# Out of the search index. A direct read by path still works.
# .cursorignore would block that, so these paths do not belong there.

# Knowledge-base articles. The overview stays searchable so a query can
# find the topic list. Open one article by path. Indexing every article
# would pull those answers into unrelated searches.
/notes/*
!/notes/00_overview.md

# local/ is gitignored. .cursorignore has the same negation, which is what
# overrides .gitignore. Repeated here so the index includes the folder.
!/local/
!/local/**
/local/.git/
/local/notes/*
!/local/notes/00_overview.md
